-- | OpenZeppelin Ownable — a standalone, token-agnostic single-owner primitive.
--
-- The Daml analogue of `Ownable.sol` / `Ownable2Step.sol`: exactly one `owner`
-- party at a time, with an explicit transfer handshake and a renounce path.
-- Independent — no role type, no dependency on the AccessControl package — so a
-- project that wants only "an owner" imports only this DAR.
--
-- # Why ownership transfer is necessarily two-step in Daml
-- In Solidity `transferOwnership(newOwner)` is a single call: the old owner
-- writes the new owner into storage. That is impossible in Daml. The owner is a
-- *signatory* of the `Ownership` contract, and a contract cannot be created
-- without the authorization of every signatory — the current owner cannot
-- unilaterally bind a new owner. So transfer is a handshake: the owner makes an
-- `OwnershipOffer`, and the prospective owner accepts it (this is exactly why
-- OpenZeppelin itself recommends `Ownable2Step`, and why this is the *only*
-- correct shape here, not merely a safer one). It also guarantees ownership
-- never lands on a party that has not actively agreed to hold it.
--
-- During a pending offer ownership is *suspended*: the `Ownership` contract is
-- archived and re-created on accept (to the new owner) or on withdraw/decline
-- (back to the current owner). Consumers that gate on "owner exists" must treat
-- the offer window accordingly.
module OpenZeppelin.Ownable where

-- | Sole ownership of a resource by `owner`.
--
-- Signatories: `owner`.
-- Observers: none; readers are granted by explicit disclosure.
-- Controllers: `owner` controls every choice.
-- Choices: `Ownership_OfferOwnership` (begin a transfer handshake),
--   `Ownership_RenounceOwnership` (leave the resource ownerless).
-- Disclosed parties: whoever the owner discloses the contract to.
-- Privacy expectations: only the owner and disclosed readers see ownership.
-- Authorization assumptions: `owner`-signed and unforgeable; only the owner
--   acts.
-- Archival behavior: `Ownership_OfferOwnership` is consuming (ownership is
--   suspended into an `OwnershipOffer`); `Ownership_RenounceOwnership` is
--   consuming and creates nothing (ownerless).
-- Failure modes: offering to the current owner is rejected (eOwnerUnchanged).
-- Upgrade and migration assumptions: 0.x, unstable; not yet public API.
template Ownership
  with
    owner : Party
      -- ^ The current sole owner.
  where
    signatory owner

    -- | Begin a two-step transfer to `newOwner`. Consuming: ownership is
    -- suspended into the returned `OwnershipOffer` until accepted, withdrawn,
    -- or declined.
    choice Ownership_OfferOwnership : ContractId OwnershipOffer
      with
        newOwner : Party
      controller owner
      do
        assertMsg eOwnerUnchanged (newOwner /= owner)
        create OwnershipOffer with owner; newOwner

    -- | Renounce ownership, leaving the resource permanently ownerless
    -- (mirrors `Ownable.renounceOwnership`). Irreversible.
    choice Ownership_RenounceOwnership : ()
      controller owner
      do
        pure ()

-- | A pending ownership transfer awaiting `newOwner`'s decision.
--
-- Signatories: `owner` (who offered). Observers: `newOwner` (who must see it to
--   accept). Controllers: `newOwner` accepts/declines; `owner` may withdraw.
-- Choices: `OwnershipOffer_Accept`, `OwnershipOffer_Decline`,
--   `OwnershipOffer_Withdraw`.
-- Disclosed parties: `owner` and `newOwner` are stakeholders.
-- Privacy expectations: limited to the two parties to the handshake.
-- Authorization assumptions: accept creates `Ownership` signed by `newOwner`,
--   so the new owner's authorization is what binds the transfer — exactly the
--   guarantee a single-step transfer could not provide.
-- Archival behavior: all three choices are consuming; accept creates the new
--   `Ownership`, withdraw/decline restore the offerer's `Ownership`.
-- Failure modes: only `newOwner` may accept/decline; only `owner` may withdraw
--   (enforced by controllers).
-- Upgrade and migration assumptions: 0.x, unstable; not yet public API.
template OwnershipOffer
  with
    owner : Party
      -- ^ The current owner who made the offer.
    newOwner : Party
      -- ^ The prospective owner who must accept.
  where
    signatory owner
    observer newOwner

    -- | Accept the transfer. Creates `Ownership` signed by `newOwner` — the new
    -- owner's authorization here is what makes the transfer sound.
    choice OwnershipOffer_Accept : ContractId Ownership
      controller newOwner
      do
        create Ownership with owner = newOwner

    -- | Decline the transfer; ownership returns to the offerer.
    choice OwnershipOffer_Decline : ContractId Ownership
      controller newOwner
      do
        create Ownership with owner

    -- | Withdraw the offer; ownership returns to the offerer.
    choice OwnershipOffer_Withdraw : ContractId Ownership
      controller owner
      do
        create Ownership with owner

-- Error messages (inlined to keep this package dependency-free).

eOwnerUnchanged : Text
eOwnerUnchanged = "Ownable: new owner is the current owner"
